{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":59,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-vector-field]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor","line":130,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Lie derivative of a $(0,k)$-tensor]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-tensor}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0062}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-vector-field}\n\n  For a $(0,k)$-tensor $T$,\n  \\[\n    ((F^t)^*T)(Y_1,\\dots,Y_k)\n      =T(DF^tY_1,\\dots,DF^tY_k)\n      =T(Y_1,\\dots,Y_k)+t(L_XT)(Y_1,\\dots,Y_k)+o(t).\n  \\]\n  This first variation defines $L_XT$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Lie derivative of a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(0,k)$\">$(0,k)$</span>-tensor] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d6c69652d646572697661746976652d74656e736f72\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0062</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-lie-derivative-vector-field\">↗ def:pet-ch2-lie-derivative-vector-field</a> <p></p>For a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(0,k)$\">$(0,k)$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T$\">$T$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-di